{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "024L", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-section-unramified}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6f7341e5f03d7cd36a9b9742843d88613d9d3b2c282cb805283413359b2e35da", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe first define ``unramified homomorphisms of local rings'' for Noetherian\nlocal rings. We cannot use the term ``unramified'' as there already is\na notion of\nan unramified ring map (Algebra, Section <REF_0001>)\nand it is different. After discussing the notion a bit we\nglobalize it to describe unramified morphisms of locally Noetherian schemes.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:794ac8b1d58d9e3fd83c80a3b677ed745cedecb62fab96f28b7e1b4a50ffe753", "unit_id": "tag:024L:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "024L", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$A$", "MATH_0002": "$B$", "MATH_0003": "$A \\to B$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathfrak m_AB = \\mathfrak m_B$", "MATH_0005": "$\\kappa(\\mathfrak m_B)$", "MATH_0006": "$\\kappa(\\mathfrak m_A)$", "MATH_0007": "$B$", "MATH_0008": "$A$", "MATH_0009": "$B$", "MATH_0010": "$A$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-unramified-rings}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ef0ed44d37c9bc052ce167677e46d7d6a316dde94d7a915dc9d274d232f503a3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:30f4b44ef372a345c83c0ad74d1393f9365df859137f693968e7f10d80267b54", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002> be Noetherian local rings. A local homomorphism <MATH_0003>\nis said to be <TEXTITOPEN_0001>unramified homomorphism of local rings<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0004>,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0005> is a finite separable extension of\n<MATH_0006>, and\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0007> is essentially of finite type over <MATH_0008> (this means\nthat <MATH_0009> is the localization of a finite type <MATH_0010>-algebra at a prime).\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:22f627b0c5e36a4b971cde2b48ac0d4d842b720878f2ee04480ae2794a1c0698", "unit_id": "tag:024M:statement"}
